post_install() {
    cat <<'TEXT'
==> greetd now runs gpui-greeter, set up in /etc/gpui-greeter/config.toml.
==> Copy the wallpapers for the Frost look:
      sudo gpui-greeter sync-wallpapers ~/Pictures/Wallpapers
==> Make greetd the display manager from the next boot, and go back:
      sudo gpui-greeter-switch greetd
      sudo gpui-greeter-switch lightdm
==> Run one display manager at a time: starting greetd while another
    display manager's session runs can end that session. To switch at
    once, log out, then on a text console run:
      sudo systemctl stop lightdm && sudo systemctl start greetd
==> The session greetd starts runs on VT 1: Ctrl+Alt+F1 returns to it
    from a text console. Stopping or restarting greetd ends it.
==> Design themes of your own with an agent: see "Theme folders" in
    /usr/share/doc/gpui-greeter/README.md
TEXT
}
